            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Does the code inside the loop run?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" hp = \" /><text value=\"-10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; hp &gt; \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; hp++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(hp);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"false\">We can't tell if the code inside the loop runs</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"true\">No, because when the loop starts, the counter variable's value is less than <code>0</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The code runs</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">No, because when the loop starts, the counter variable's value is less than <code>0</code>.</p></body></html>"
